# Omabuntu shell login autostart (plan 012, Option A: pure autostart).
# Deployed to ~/.config/systemd/user/omabuntu-shell.service by
# tools/deploy_autostart.py. Enabled only after explicit user approval.
# No Restart directive: the shell starts once per login and is never a
# supervisor. The manager's running.json record stays the source of truth
# for the owned process; use `omabuntu stop`, not `systemctl --user stop`,
# to end the shell mid-session (stopping the unit would kill the process
# group at logout through PartOf, which is the intended session lifetime).
[Unit]
Description=Omabuntu shell login autostart hand-off
PartOf=graphical-session.target
Requires=graphical-session.target
After=graphical-session.target
ConditionEnvironment=WAYLAND_DISPLAY

[Service]
Type=oneshot
RemainAfterExit=no
ExecStart=%h/.local/bin/omabuntu start
Slice=session.slice

[Install]
WantedBy=graphical-session.target
